  {
    "ply": 13,
    "san": "Qg4",
    "comment": "Theory advices 7.Bxe7.\nLilienthal, with the move in the text, preferres a poisoned continuation.\nAfterward Paul Keres stopped any discussion on the subject with his\ndeclaration: \"After 7.Qg4 White is better.\" Full stop. Now Black must do his\nsteps very carefully.",
    "nags": []
  },
  {
    "ply": 14,
    "san": "f5",
    "comment": "Lilienthal: \"Afterward, during the Second\nInternational Tournament in Moscow, Vera Menchik, in the same position, played\nagainst me 7... Nc6 but after 8. Bxe7 Kxe7 9. Qg5+ Kf8 10. Qxd8+ Nxd8 11. f4 I\nhad advantage.\"  Preferable to Spielmann's move is however 7... Kf8 with the\npossible continuation 8. Nf3 Nc6 9. Qf4 cxd4 10. Nb5 a6 11. Nbxd4 Nc5",
    "nags": []
